<title>ITALY: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>ITALY GOVERNMENT LIST (961114)</p>
<p> President................................Oscar Luigi SCALFARO</p>
<p>(Sworn in 28 May 92 for a seven-year term)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT (Sworn in 18 May 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister...................................Romano PRODI</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.........................Walter VELTRONI</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Culture)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture.....................................Michele PINTO</p>
<p> Culture.............................See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p> Defence...................................Beniamino ANDREATTA</p>
<p> Education &amp; Technology.......................Luigi BERLINGUER</p>
<p> Environment........................................Edo RONCHI</p>
<p> Equal Opportunites...........................Anna FINOCCHIARO</p>
<p> Finance........................................Vincenzo VISCO</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs.................................Lamberto DINI</p>
<p> Foreign Trade................................Augusto FANTOZZI</p>
<p> Health..........................................Rosaria BINDI</p>
<p> Industry &amp; Tourism..........................Pierluigi BERSANI</p>
<p> Interior...................................Giorgio NAPOLITANO</p>
<p> Justice..................................Giovanni Maria FLICK</p>
<p> Labour...........................................Tiziano TREU</p>
<p> Post &amp; Communications.......................Antonio MACCANICO</p>
<p> Public Works..............................Antonio DI PIETRO**</p>
<p>						    (**Resigned 14 Nov 96)</p>
<p> Regional affairs.............................Franco BASSANINI</p>
<p> Transport....................................Claudio BURLANDO</p>
<p> Treasury &amp; Budget........................Carlo Azeglio CIAMPI</p>
<p> Social Affairs....................................Livia TURCO</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Speaker of the Senate..........................Nicola MANCINO</p>
<p> Speaker of the Chamber of Deputies...........Luciano VIOLANTE</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor...........................Antonio FAZIO</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
